============================================================================================
PART 3 -- measured regime-2 constants and the corrected composition
============================================================================================
  max rho upper-bracket over battery: 9.335
  min |G'| over battery: 0.01216

  CORRECTED COMPLEMENTARITY (for HYP-6830):
  - r_P <= B(c*) is FALSE as phrased: scale-free cores fragment ~linearly in height
    (r_P tracks Sum(P); divisibility is not the only fragmentation source).
  - The TRUE regime-2 invariant is the RATIO rho = v*/maxP = r_P/(pi |G'| maxP):
    * dilates multiply r_P and maxP by c together -> rho is scale-INVARIANT;
    * spread cores: r_P ~ alpha*Sum(P) and |G'| bounded below -> rho = O(1);
    * so the band (maxP, v*] is bounded RELATIVE to the core everywhere tested,
      max ratio ~9.4 at the {1..12} shape (dilates of it inherit 9.33).
  - Proof obligation that remains: |G'_P| >= floor(shape) for 12-cores off the
    classified tight families (stability around rigidity, mac-mini B5 lane),
    which converts rho = O(1) from measured to proved via r_P <= Sum(P).
